Below is an example Azure DevOps YAML stage that uses a Bash script to download a Terraform Enterprise (TFE) state file from Azure Blob Storage (using the az CLI), âmergesâuploads the updated file back to Azure, and then publishes that file as a pipeline artifact. (Adjust container names, storage account names and keys, blob names, and merge log
ic as needed.)

Note:
â¢ This example assumes that your state file is JSON and that merging two state files is as simple as âmergingâ
â¢ It also assumes that the build agent already has the az CLI and jq installed.
â¢ You may want to store your storage credentials (or use a Service Connection) via pipeline variables or Azure DevOps Service Connections.
